From 7cc243cda5ce654d3a58e17bc6554f9b06abe75a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 16:17:12 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] gnome-shell-manager: don't ungrab accelerators we never
 grabbed

grab_single_accelerator() deliberately refuses to bind XF86PowerOff, so
that the shell's own screen-saver-manager keeps the power key and can
blank the screen. It still records an AcceleratorInfo and hands the
caller an action id, because g-s-d should go on handling every other
key.

The free path is not as careful. Whenever that info is disposed of --
g-s-d ungrabbing, re-grabbing its set after a settings change, or simply
going away -- free_accelerator_info_from_hash_table() calls
remove_action_entries() for the accelerator unconditionally. Both sides
key the shell's one global action group by the accelerator's name, so
that removes screen-saver-manager's action and sends the compositor an
ungrab for a binding this code never owned.

The power key is then dead for the rest of the session, silently: the
grab did succeed, so nothing is logged, and the compositor simply has no
accelerator registered for the keysym any more. The key still wakes a
blanked screen, because that is the idle-activity path rather than an
accelerator, which makes it look like the shell is ignoring only some
presses.

Remember whether we registered the action, and only remove it if we did.

Assisted-by: Claude
Signed-off-by: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
---
 src/gnome-shell-manager.c | 11 ++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/gnome-shell-manager.c b/src/gnome-shell-manager.c
index 854aa24..3010b83 100644
--- a/src/gnome-shell-manager.c
+++ b/src/gnome-shell-manager.c
@@ -71,6 +71,7 @@ typedef struct _AcceleratorInfo {
   guint                            mode_flags;
   guint                            grab_flags;
   guint                            repeat_id;
+  gboolean                         registered;
 } AcceleratorInfo;
 
 static void
@@ -89,7 +90,14 @@ free_accelerator_info_from_hash_table (gpointer data)
   AcceleratorInfo *info = (AcceleratorInfo *) data;
   g_return_if_fail (info != NULL);
 
-  remove_action_entries (info->accelerator);
+  /*
+   * Only take back what we put there. The shell registers accelerators of
+   * its own in the same action group, keyed by the same name, so removing
+   * one we never added -- see grab_single_accelerator() skipping the power
+   * key -- ungrabs the shell's own binding out from under it.
+   */
+  if (info->registered)
+    remove_action_entries (info->accelerator);
   g_clear_handle_id (&info->repeat_id, g_source_remove);
   g_free (info->accelerator);
   g_free (info->sender);
@@ -204,6 +212,7 @@ grab_single_accelerator (PhoshGnomeShellManager *self,
                                                     action_entries,
                                                     G_N_ELEMENTS (action_entries),
                                                     info);
+    info->registered = TRUE;
   } else {
     /*
      * FIXME: Don't allow binding of power keys so we can blank the screen
-- 
2.55.0

